# __DISPLAY_NAME__

PySide6 Qt Widgets application managed by `uv`. Edit UI layout only in Qt Designer `.ui` files; regenerate `*_ui.py` after every UI change.

## Develop

```powershell
uv sync
uv run python scripts/compile_ui.py
uv run pytest
uv run __PROJECT_NAME__
```

Validate UI/View naming without regenerating files:

```powershell
uv run python scripts/compile_ui.py --check
```

## Build

```powershell
uv build
uv run python scripts/package_app.py --profile minimal
```

The packaging wrapper performs a clean PyInstaller build, rejects unnecessary Qt runtime modules/plugins, and runs a hidden packaged-app smoke test. The executable is written under `dist/__PROJECT_NAME__/`.

Use `--profile full` only after intentionally adding QML, Quick, PDF, OpenGL, SVG, VirtualKeyboard, Qt Network, localization, or extra plugin features. Inspect an existing runtime tree with:

```powershell
uv run python scripts/audit_package.py dist/__PROJECT_NAME__ --profile minimal
```
